{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nPurpose: conservative module-wide Terraform evidence for T10 Pass 1 and independent Pass 2.\n\n## Scope\n\n### Optional boundary\n\nAdd `grounding-terraform = [\"python-hcl2==8.1.3\"]` and the `hcl2` probe. In `_capabilities.py`, add `grounding-terraform` to `DECLARED_EXTRAS` and register ABSTAIN-posture `grounding_terraform`. It is sole opt-in; core/non-Terraform paths import/advertise nothing. Extend optionality CI.\n\n### Structural index\n\nAdd `terraform_index.py`/`terraform_tools.py`. Each call owns cache+ledger; its finalizer frees them. Pass 2 re-captures the frozen source; no cache crosses steps.\n\n- Trigger on impacted `.tf`/`.tf.json`, or Terraform/OpenTofu plan plus repo Terraform. Index affected directories; follow repo-contained literal children/reverse callers; exclude VCS, virtualenv, `.terraform/`.\n- Directly inspect a changed `.tfvars`, but never infer it is selected.\n- Reject absolute/out-of-repo sources and escaping symlinks. Enforce 64 modules, 5,000 files, 32 MiB, and the existing 60-second deadline before returning facts; any failure yields one abstention with no partial facts.\n- Exact-wheel import probe exited 0: `8.1.3`; `parses_to_tree` signature `(text: str) -> lark.tree.Tree`; `parser().options.propagate_positions=True`; `Tree.meta` block `(1,1,3,2)`, attribute `(2,2,2,15)`; serialized meta keys `['__is_block__']`. Use `parses_to_tree` on strict-UTF-8-decoded bytes; JSON uses unambiguous key range, else file-level. Full command/output: ticket evidence comment dated 2026-09-03.\n\n### Operations and schemas\n\n- `lookup_declaration(address, module_path=\"\")`: variable, local, output, module, provider, managed resource, data resource.\n- `resolve_reference(reference, from_file)`: direct module traversals/repo-local child outputs; resource bases may resolve, provider attributes never do.\n- Both are `job=refute`: static resolution returns `refuted` at T1; all non-proof is `abstain`; neither emits `match` or asserts absence.\n- Grounding references use `kind=\"symbol\"` for declarations and `kind=\"member\"` for dotted traversals, with canonical address as `name` and `language=\"terraform\"`. Closed `terraform_kind`: `variable|local|output|module|provider|managed_resource|data_resource`.\n- Normalize paths to NFC repo-relative POSIX (empty module `.`; collapse dots; preserve case; reject NUL/absolute/escaping `..`). Trim outer address whitespace, grammar-parse, and case-preserving dot-render; internal whitespace, splats, or computed indexes abstain.\n\nAdd closed `terraform_grounding_receipt.schema.json`; validate evidence against `grounding.schema.json` and receipts against it. Required receipt fields: `schema_version`, `operation`, normalized `query`, `snapshot_digest`, `module_digest`, `backend` (parser/version, analyzer/version, config digest), `limits`, `outcome`, generic `reason`, closed `reason_detail`, and `result_digest`. Snapshot/module SHA-256 uses a sorted length-prefixed path+byte stream. Config/result reuse `\"sha256:\" + rebar._store.canonical.content_hash(float_free_object)`. Refuted hashes safe facts; abstain hashes exactly `{outcome,reason,reason_detail}`.\n\nWorked receipt (digests abbreviated only here):\n\n`{\"schema_version\":1,\"operation\":\"lookup_declaration\",\"query\":{\"address\":\"module.web\",\"module\":\"infra\"},\"snapshot_digest\":\"sha256:…\",\"module_digest\":\"sha256:…\",\"backend\":{\"parser\":\"python-hcl2\",\"parser_version\":\"8.1.3\",\"analyzer\":\"rebar-terraform-structural\",\"analyzer_version\":1,\"config_digest\":\"sha256:…\"},\"limits\":{\"modules\":64,\"files\":5000,\"bytes\":33554432,\"timeout_ms\":60000},\"outcome\":\"refuted\",\"reason\":null,\"reason_detail\":null,\"result_digest\":\"sha256:…\"}`\n\nWorked abstain (same required provenance): `{\"operation\":\"resolve_reference\",\"query\":{\"reference\":\"aws_instance.web.id\",\"from_file\":\"infra/main.tf\"},\"outcome\":\"abstain\",\"reason\":\"ambiguous\",\"reason_detail\":\"provider_attribute\",\"result_digest\":\"sha256:…\"}`.\n\nExact abstention translation:\n\n- Missing extra → `no_tool/missing_extra`; wrong parser version → `version_skew/parser_version`; non-Terraform call → `unsupported_lang/not_terraform`.\n- Pre-worker invalid/undecodable input → `parse_error/invalid_input`; unreadable capture → `parse_error/unreadable_file`.\n- Harness `timeout` → `timeout/worker_timeout`; harness `parse_error` (including indistinguishable native signal death) → `parse_error/invalid_input`; harness `other` from raise/no-result/protocol failure → `other/worker_failure`.\n- Duplicate address → `ambiguous/duplicate_address`; no unique hit → `ambiguous/no_unique_address`; dynamic source/expression → `ambiguous/dynamic_source|dynamic_expression`; computed value → `ambiguous/computed_value`; provider attribute → `ambiguous/provider_attribute`; splat/index → `ambiguous/splat_index`; unknown tfvars selection → `ambiguous/unknown_tfvars`.\n- Absolute/out-of-repo/escaping symlink → `private_or_internal_suspected/path_outside_snapshot`.\n- Module/file/byte bound → `other/module_limit|file_limit|byte_limit`.\n\nReturn only safe classes, hashes, and repo-relative locations—never credentials or literal payloads.\n\n### Plan-review integration\n\nInject tools only into Terraform T10 Pass 1. Terraform evidence selects Pass 2 with a fresh ledger and required independent query; inject no Pass-1 answer. Add a per-call tool provider/finalizer to `RunnerAgentStep`, preserving static `extra_tools`.\n\nRecord concrete reads as synthetic `read_file` usage and signed `**/*.tf`/`**/*.tf.json` membership, so sibling additions alter stdlib-only freshness. Missing extra exposes no tools; failures abstain.\n\n## Positive rationale\n\nReuse existing seams; never scan or evaluate Terraform.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nRegistry/remote content, prompts, scanners, `terraform-config-inspect`, and Terraform/OpenTofu/provider execution.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Lean-install tests pin `python-hcl2==8.1.3`; absent-extra/non-Terraform routes import/advertise nothing.\n- [ ] Index tests find sibling files, bounded child/reverse callers, and keep targeted `.tfvars` unselected.\n- [ ] `lookup_declaration` tests assert exact `symbol`/`terraform_kind`, T1 `refuted`, line range, safe facts, and receipt.\n- [ ] `resolve_reference` tests assert exact `member` mapping and child-output resolution; computed/provider/dynamic controls abstain.\n- [ ] Boundary tests assert exact reasons/digests, no partial facts, cache/ledger retirement, worker reaping, and below/at/above bounds.\n- [ ] Workflow integration captures T10 Pass-1/Pass-2 requests with distinct ledgers; non-T10/non-Terraform controls expose no tool.\n- [ ] Signed-read-set tests observe all parsed files/patterns, then add a sibling `.tf` and observe freshness change.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_tools.py::test_no_forbidden_executables` observes no Terraform, OpenTofu, provider, tfparse, TFLint, Trivy, terraform-ls, terraform-docs, or other executable.\n- [ ] Schema tests validate evidence/receipts; `docs/grounding.md` and ADR 0111 document tools, trust boundary, outcomes/reasons, posture, limits, lifecycle, and prohibitions.\n\n## Testing\n\nTest contract card:\n\n- Contract: REB-640, `docs/grounding.md`, ADR 0111, both schemas, harness `RunResult`.\n- Preconditions: sibling/child/reverse, dynamic, escape, bound, and harness fixtures.\n- Production: real capture/worker/response/request; fake only the model.\n- Tiers: parser/evidence unit-contract; workflow integration; lean-install subprocess.\n- Oracles: exact evidence/receipt/tools; no partial facts; cleanup; membership-digest change.\n- Controls: non-Terraform has no tools; literal resolves, computed abstains.\n- CI: `make test`, `make docs-check`, and optionality CI.\n\n## Verification\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_index.py tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_tools.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py tests/unit/test_capabilities.py && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make docs-check`"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788478285649273630,"uuid":"f98cc40b-8345-4394-a2db-7b703b8dae22"}